numericalRank -- numerical rank of a matrix
*******************************************

  * Usage: 
        r = numericalRank M
        B = isFullNumericalRank M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a matrix with real or complex
        entries
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Threshold => ..., default value .0001
  * Outputs:
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * B, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,

Description
===========

*note numericalRank: numericalRank, finds an approximate rank of the matrix M.

*note isFullNumericalRank: numericalRank, = M is _not_ rank-deficient.

Let \sigma_1,...,\sigma_n be the singular values of M. 

If *note Threshold: (LLLBases)Threshold, is >1, then to establish numerical
rank we look for the first large gap between two consecutive singular values.
The gap between \sigma_i and \sigma_{i+1} is large if \sigma_i/\sigma_{i+1} >
*note Threshold: (LLLBases)Threshold,.

If *note Threshold: (LLLBases)Threshold, is <=1, then the rank equals the
number of singular values larger then *note Threshold: (LLLBases)Threshold,.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : options numericalRank                  |
|                                            |
|o1 = OptionTable{Threshold => .0001}        |
|                                            |
|o1 : OptionTable                            |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : numericalRank matrix {{2,1},{0,0.001}} |
|                                            |
|o2 = 2                                      |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : numericalRank matrix {{2,1},{0,0.0001}}|
|                                            |
|o3 = 1                                      |
+--------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

We assume \sigma_0=1 above.

See also
========

  * *note SVD: (Macaulay2Doc)SVD, -- singular value decomposition of a matrix

